    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.attribute_mixing_dict - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.attribute_mixing_dict.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.attribute_mixing_dict()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Count edges by the attribute values of their two endpoints.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.attribute_mixing_dict()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Count edges by the attribute values of their two endpoints.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.attribute_mixing_dict()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Count edges by the attribute values of their two endpoints.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nCount edges by the attribute values of their two endpoints.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L42517-L42598){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.attribute_mixing_dict(\n    attribute,\n    normalized=False,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Attribute mixing dict](../assets/graphs/attribute-mixing-dict.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Two triangles joined by one edge, with team x on A, B, C (teal) and team y on D, E, F (violet). Each triangle's three edges count from both ends, 6 within each team, and the one accent edge C–D links x to y once each way: {x: {x: 6, y: 1}, y: {x: 1, y: 6}}.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nFor every pair of values `(a, b)` of a categorical node attribute, how many edges run\nfrom a node with value `a` to a node with value `b`. This is the basis of homophily\nanalysis: in a friendship network split by school year or party, most edges stay within\na group if like links with like. Undirected edges count from both ends (so the table is\nsymmetric); directed edges count once, source value first. See\n`attribute_mixing_matrix()` for a matrix and `assortativity_nominal()` for the\nsingle-number summary. Matches NetworkX's `attribute_mixing_dict()`.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[attribute]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Name of the node attribute. Every node must have a value.\n\n<code>[normalized]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, return fractions of all counted edge ends instead of counts. Default is\n    `False`.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [dict]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   A nested dictionary `{a: {b: count}}`, both levels sorted (by their text if values\n    are not comparable).\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If some node has no value for the attribute.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~attribute_mixing_matrix`) \n\n:   The same counts as a matrix.\n\n[](`~assortativity_nominal`) \n\n:   One number for how much like links with like.\n\n[](`~degree_mixing_dict`) \n\n:   Count links by degree instead.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nEach link counts once from each end, so the one link between the teams, `B`–`C`, counts\nonce for each:\n\n::: {#294bdbbc .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\")])\ngraph = graph.set_node_attrs(\n    \"team\", {\"A\": \"red\", \"B\": \"red\", \"C\": \"blue\", \"D\": \"blue\"}\n)\n\ngraph.attribute_mixing_dict(\"team\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n{'blue': {'blue': 2, 'red': 1}, 'red': {'blue': 1, 'red': 2}}\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Across the clubs\n\n`friends()` links 24 members of two clubs in a made-up town, a chess club and a climbing\nclub, who are friends. Counted from both ends, 76 of the 86 ends of friendships stay\nwithin a club. The five friendships across the clubs all involve Hugo, from the chess\nclub, or Tara, a climber, the couple at the center of the network:\n\n::: {#7faded54 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfriends = ec.friends()\nclub = friends.get_node_attrs(\"club\")\nlabel = friends.get_label_from_id\nacross = [\n    (label(s), label(t))\n    for _, s, t in friends.get_edges_as_tuples() if club[s] != club[t]\n]\n\nfriends.attribute_mixing_dict(\"club\"), across\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n({'Chess': {'Chess': 40, 'Climbing': 5},\n  'Climbing': {'Chess': 5, 'Climbing': 36}},\n [('Hugo', 'Tara'),\n  ('Tara', 'Ben'),\n  ('Tara', 'Jules'),\n  ('Hugo', 'Oona'),\n  ('Hugo', 'Wes')])\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#823bc62b .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfriends.plot(\n    highlight=across, color_by=\"club\", edge_color_by=\"club\",\n    label_by=\"label\", seed=8,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-8b5e09c7:#52525b;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-8b5e09c7:#a1a1aa;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-8b5e09c7:#52525b;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-8b5e09c7:#a1a1aa;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"700\" height=\"500\" viewBox=\"14.0 -37.1 833.0 595.0\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSyste